No blocker: PR #99 can be merged as it stands. The fixes I found are small, so they go in PUBLIC PR 1's first commit, and five more are findings to record. I reviewed alone, from the commit objects only. CI was green on head `20531c2c`, the PR was CLEAN, and the head had not moved at the end.

The five most important:

1. **Should-fix: the attendance card loses its partial line on a network failure, a timeout or a 429.** The card says "the capacity was saved, the settings were not" through the form's failure title. The shared form code drops that title for those three failures, so the owner is never told the capacity was saved. Finding 96 is marked resolved on exactly this behaviour, so you may prefer a fix round on this PR instead of waiting.
2. **Should-fix: a 404 on the staff, settings and capacity routes doesn't refresh the owner's spaces.** Since carried item 7 the packages' routes do this, so the space switcher stops offering a space whose link ended. The two new pages don't. Doing it would make a third copy of `useLinkEnded`, so whether that hook moves to `shared/` is your call.
3. **Should-fix, plausible: a staff account whose answer was lost can't be recovered from the page.** If the connection drops after the server creates the account, the owner retries and is told the email already has an account. The list is never read again, so the new row, with its "new temporary password" action, doesn't appear. I traced this in the code but didn't run it.
4. **Nit, plausible: switching the interface language can save the default reminder as the space's own text.** The comparison uses the default text of the language the page opened in. After a switch, saving the untouched card sends the English default instead of keeping it empty. Traced, not run.
5. **Nit: three small document mismatches.** `occupancy.md` still says "no web screen yet". `users.md` keeps its old Last Updated date. A blank line splits the list of decisions in `space-links.md`.

The rest are small nits: a misplaced comment in the English copy, a loading state a screen reader can't hear, and two alerts when the settings fail to load. The findings to record (numbered 103 onward) are:
- the Arabic-digit readers, now five copies;
- `useMenuTriggers` copying the admin page's `useRowTriggers`;
- held menu items possibly unreachable by keyboard. This is the project-wide menu pattern; I didn't open Radix's source to confirm it.
- two lines from the approved copy: the "now has another space" refusal is also shown when the account has become an admin's, and the insert buttons' names don't contain the text they show.

I accepted every departure in the executor's report. Everything I only read in their report, and didn't check myself, is listed in the review. That covers the local test runs, the breaks, the real run and its screenshots.

